  "node": {
    "id": "ctkg:v3e-object-d4f2962cd7855d13327cecbb",
    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "滞后校正提高了低于两个转折频率处的幅值，从而减小稳态误差；或者可用于降低转折频率之上的幅值，以获得满意的相角裕度。它在两个转折频率之间产生相位滞后，并且通常比超前校正具有更慢的响应。",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "Lag compensation increases magnitude at frequencies below two break points, decreasing steady-state errors, or can be used to decrease magnitude above break points to achieve acceptable PM. It contributes phase lag between break points and typically provides slower response than lead compensation.",
